            },
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": " 作“真实的，真正的”解，是指所形容的物品的外貌与实际情况相符，或某种事物是客观存在的，不是虚假的。"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "c2",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": "It is a "
            },
            {
              "t": "underline",
              "v": "real"
            },
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": " diamond. 这是一颗真钻石。"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "c3",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": "He was asked to give his "
            },
            {
              "t": "underline",
              "v": "real"
            },
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": " reason for being late. 他被要求说出迟到的真实理由。"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "c4",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "t": "strong",
              "v": "true"
            },
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": " 作“真的，确实的”解，是指和事实相符。形容人时，是指“忠实的”。"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "c5",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": "This is a "
            },
            {
              "t": "underline",
              "v": "true"
            },
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": " story in real life. 这是现实生活的真实故事。"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "c6",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": "A "
            },
            {
              "t": "underline",
              "v": "true"
            },
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": " friend is one who will always stand by you when in need. 真正的朋友总是在需要时站在你身边的。"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "c7",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "t": "strong",
              "v": "actual"
            },
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": " 作“实际的，现实的”解，是指所形容之物在事实上已发生和存在。"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "c8",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": "In "
            },
            {
              "t": "underline",
              "v": "actual"
            },
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": " life, things are not so simple. 在现实生活中，事情总没那么简单。"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "c9",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "t": "strong",
              "v": "genuine"
            },
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": " 作“真正的，非伪造的”解，是指所形容之物是地道的，不是冒充的，以及所形容的感情是真诚的，而不是虚伪的。"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "c10",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": "It’s a "
            },
            {
              "t": "underline",
              "v": "genuine"
            },
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": " Picasso. 这是一幅毕加索的真迹。"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "c11",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": "He showed "
            },
            {
              "t": "underline",
              "v": "genuine"
            },
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": " sorrow at the death of his dog. 狗死的时候，他流露出真实的悲伤。"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
